# Sandbox anchor

Starting tree for the scenarios that need a real GitHub remote. Kept to what a
scenario actually reads, so the tree stays small enough to eyeball.

`utils.js` is the file the `git:pr`, `git:issue`, and `git:followup` scenarios
append to. The other six either write their own tree or wipe this one first.

Dropped from the tree the anchor remote used to carry, because nothing reads it:
a `package.json`, an application scaffold, and any `.claude/` content, which the
injection flags provide when a scenario asks for it.
